---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {Header,Footer} from '../../components/ui';
import ListeningDemo from '../../components/ListeningDemo';
import {getPracticeLanguages} from '../../lib/content';
import '../../styles/growth.css';
const english=getPracticeLanguages().find(l=>l.id==='en')!;
---
<Base title="Practice Minimal Pairs Without Building an Anki Deck | MinimalPairs" description="Want minimal-pair listening practice without finding audio or building flashcards? Try English and French sound challenges directly in your browser.">
 <Header/><main class="growth-page"><header class="growth-hero"><p class="eyebrow">MINIMAL-PAIR LISTENING PRACTICE</p><h1>Less time making cards.<br/><em>More time hearing the difference.</em></h1><p class="growth-lede">If you want to practice minimal pairs without building an Anki deck, start here. Pick a sound, press play, and get feedback.</p><div class="growth-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="#try">Try a free round →</a><a href="/english-minimal-pairs">Browse English sounds →</a><a href="/french-minimal-pairs">Browse French sounds →</a></div></header>
 <section class="growth-grid" id="try"><div><h2>Ship or sheep?<br/><em>Hear more than the spelling.</em></h2><p>A minimal pair changes one sound: <strong>ship</strong> /ʃɪp/ and <strong>sheep</strong> /ʃip/, for example.</p><p>The challenge takes that a step further. Hear two reference words, then a different word in another voice. Decide which reference shares the sound in the new word.</p><p>Press play on A, B and X. Match the target vowel. You can listen again before choosing.</p><a href="/learn/en-i-ih">Explore ship vs sheep with audio and IPA →</a></div><ListeningDemo client:visible language={english} contrastId="en-i-ih"/></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>Use the tool that fits the job.</h2><div class="growth-steps"><article><h3>Keep Anki for your own cards</h3><p>If you enjoy choosing examples, creating cards and managing your deck, a personal flashcard collection gives you that control.</p></article><article><h3>Use MinimalPairs to start listening</h3><p>The sound groups and recordings are already organized. Choose a lesson or take the diagnostic to find a starting point.</p></article><article><h3>Combine them</h3><p>Practice a sound difference here, then continue learning vocabulary in the system you already use. You don’t need to move your existing deck.</p></article></div></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>A clear next step after each session.</h2><p>During practice, hear feedback after answering and continue with new examples. Use sound matching to focus on listening, or word identification to connect sounds and spelling.</p><p>The diagnostic gives you a snapshot of the contrasts you matched. Premium adds the detailed report and full lesson library so you can work on what you missed.</p><div class="growth-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/diagnostic/en">Find my English starting point →</a><a href="/diagnostic/fr">Try the French listening check →</a></div></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>Which sounds do you want to hear clearly?</h2><div class="growth-steps"><article><h3>French: tu or tout?</h3><p>Practice /y/ and /u/, then explore nasal vowels and other French sound contrasts.</p><a href="/challenge/tu-vs-tout">Try tu vs tout →</a></article><article><h3>English: ship or sheep?</h3><p>Compare /ɪ/ and /i/ across different words and voices.</p><a href="/challenge/ship-vs-sheep">Try ship vs sheep →</a></article><article><h3>Not sure where to begin?</h3><p>Take a short listening check, see your overall score, and choose your next practice.</p><a href="/diagnostic/fr">Check French →</a><br/><a href="/diagnostic/en">Check English →</a></article></div></section>
 <section class="growth-price"><div><strong>Lifetime access. Every current practice language.</strong><p>Premium covers all current practice languages. Start with the free listening check and lessons.</p></div><a class="button button-dark" href="/pricing">Explore Premium →</a></section>
 <section class="growth-section"><h2>Try another sound.</h2><div class="growth-links"><a href="/challenge/right-vs-light">Right vs light →</a><a href="/challenge/thin-vs-sin">Thin vs sin →</a><a href="/challenge/tu-vs-tout">Tu vs tout →</a></div><p class="growth-source">MinimalPairs is an independent browser app. Anki is a separate product; this is not an Anki add-on or an exportable deck.</p></section>
 </main><Footer/>
</Base>
